From: Surface Go Gaming OS
Subject: [PATCH] Finalize the platform while its WebKit backend is alive

Cog 0.18.5 destroys the shell and WebKitWebViewBackend before finalizing
the Wayland platform. The backend destroy notifier has then freed the FDO
exportable which platform finalization still uses to release the displayed
image. Finalize the platform first, with the shell/backend still alive.

This is the lifetime-order correction reported in upstream issue 744, not
a replacement quit path or a change to crash status handling.
Upstream: https://github.com/Igalia/cog/issues/744

--- a/launcher/cog-launcher.c
+++ b/launcher/cog-launcher.c
@@ -457,6 +457,13 @@
 {
     CogLauncher *launcher = COG_LAUNCHER(object);
 
+    /* The platform releases images through the shell's WebKit backend.
+     * Its destroy notifier must not run until that cleanup is complete.
+     */
+    CogPlatform *platform = cog_platform_get_default();
+    if (platform)
+        g_object_unref(platform);
+
     if (launcher->shell) {
         g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func(launcher->shell, G_CALLBACK(on_notify_web_view), NULL);
         g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func(launcher->shell, G_CALLBACK(cog_launcher_create_view), NULL);
@@ -479,8 +486,6 @@
     g_clear_pointer(&launcher->net_mem_settings, webkit_memory_pressure_settings_free);
 #endif /* COG_HAVE_MEM_PRESSURE */
 
-    g_object_unref(cog_platform_get_default());
-
     G_OBJECT_CLASS(cog_launcher_parent_class)->dispose(object);
 }
 
